## Approach

Factor tree-sitter parser lifecycle out of individual adapters into core-owned infrastructure. Introduce a `ParseContext` struct that provides the already-parsed tree to adapters, a `ParserPool` that reuses one `Parser` per language across files, and a configurable timeout via `Parser::set_timeout_micros`. Adapters gain a `grammar()` method returning their `tree_sitter::Language` and their `parse()` method receives `&ParseContext` instead of raw `(source, file_path)`. The pool is created per parse run (full or incremental) and threaded through `parse_single_file`.

This keeps the pool lifetime simple (no cross-thread sharing needed since parsing is sequential per workspace) and the adapter contract clean (adapters do extraction, core owns the parser).

