### Step 4: Refactor rust.rs::parse — remove parser creation, receive ParseContext

Change signature and remove the first 12 lines (Parser::new through root_node). The extraction logic stays identical:

```rust
use super::adapter::ParseContext;

pub fn parse(ctx: &ParseContext) -> Result<ParseResult> {
    let root = ctx.tree.root_node();
    let parsed_ok = !root.has_error();
    let src = ctx.source;

    let mut symbols = Vec::new();
    collect_symbols(&mut symbols, root, src, &[]);

    let mut references = Vec::new();
    collect_references(&mut references, root, src);

    let mut imports = Vec::new();
    collect_imports(&mut imports, root, src);

    Ok(ParseResult {
        file_path: ctx.file_path.to_string(),
        language: "rust".to_string(),
        symbols,
        references,
        imports,
        parsed_ok,
        line_count: std::str::from_utf8(src)
            .map(|s| s.lines().count())
            .unwrap_or(0),
    })
}
```

Remove the `use tree_sitter::Parser;` import (keep `Node`, `TreeCursor` which are still used by extraction).

